**************************************** Migration Command *******************************************************

1. Create a new table with migration
php artisan make:migration create_products_table

public function up()
{
    Schema::create('products', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->id();
        $table->string('name');
        $table->integer('price');
        $table->tinyInteger('status')->byDefault(1);
        $table->unsignedBigInteger('created_by');
        $table->softDeletes();

        $table->foreign('created_by')->references('id')->on('admins')->onDelete('cascade');
        $table->timestamps();
    });
}

public function down()
{
    Schema::dropIfExists('products');
}


2. Create a table with model + migration
php artisan make:model Product -m

public function up()
{
    Schema::create('products', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->id();
        $table->string('title');
        $table->timestamps();
    });
}

public function down()
{
    Schema::dropIfExists('products');
}


3. Add a new column in an existing table (as foreign key)
php artisan make:migration add_category_id_to_products_table --table=products

public function up()
{
    Schema::table('products', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->foreignId('category_id')->references('id')->on('categories')->onDelete('cascade');
    });
}

public function down()
{
    Schema::table('products', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->dropForeign(['category_id']);
        $table->dropColumn('category_id');
    });
}



4. Add a column after a specific column
php artisan make:migration add_statuc_column_in_products_table --table=products


public function up()
{
    Schema::table('products', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->string('status')->after('price');
    });
}

public function down()
{
    Schema::table('products', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->dropColumn('status');
    });
}



5. Run a specific migration file
php artisan migrate --path=/database/migrations/2025_01_01_123456_create_products_table.php










1. What is a migration in Laravel?
Migration is a version control system for the database. It helps you create, update, or delete tables using PHP code instead of SQL.

2. Why do we use migrations?
To keep database structure in sync across all environments and team members.

3. What is the difference between up() and down() in migration?
up() → applies changes (create/modify table)

down() → undo changes (drop/revert table)

4. How to rollback last migration?
php artisan migrate:rollback

5. How to rollback all migrations?
php artisan migrate:reset


6. How to refresh all migrations?
php artisan migrate:refresh


7. How to check migration status?
php artisan migrate:status


8. What is a migration batch?
A batch is a group of migrations executed together in one run.

9. Which migrations rollback when we run migrate:rollback?
Only the latest batch of migrations.
